# A token is what the text that makes it says (CR 612.4, 111.4), and an activated ability's text is fixed as it is activated
# (CR 602.2): it exists independently of its source (CR 113.7a), and a text-changing effect changes the permanent it affects
# (CR 612.1), not the ability on the stack. Bot1 activates Thopter Foundry ("Create a 1/1 blue Thopter") and in response
# Sleight of Mind replaces blue with red in the Foundry's text: the ability still makes a blue Thopter. The Foundry's own
# text says red from then on (its control is trait-doctoring-changes-the-color-of-the-tokens-thopter-foundry-makes), so the
# Thopter its next activation makes the same turn is red.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Thopter Foundry
Mox Pearl
Sleight of Mind
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thopter Foundry.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Thopter Foundry.Activate(Sacrifice: Mox Pearl)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sleight of Mind.Cast(Thopter Foundry)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Thopter Token.Colors = Blue
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Thopter Foundry.Activate(Sacrifice: Mox Ruby)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Thopter Token#1.Colors = Blue
Bot1.Battlefield.Thopter Token#2.Colors = Red
